    {
      "kind": "finish",
      "args": {
        "summary": "Fixed a bug in astropy v5.3 where NDDataRef mask propagation failed when performing arithmetic operations between an NDDataRef object with a mask and one without a mask, specifically when using `handle_mask=np.bitwise_or`. \n\nThe issue was in the `_arithmetic_mask` method in `/testbed/astropy/nddata/mixins/ndarithmetic.py`. The method had logic to handle cases where `self.mask` was None, but it was missing the symmetric case where `operand.mask` was None while `self.mask` existed. This caused `np.bitwise_or` to be called with a None value, resulting in a TypeError.\n\nThe fix adds an additional `elif` clause to handle the case where `operand.mask is None and self.mask is not None`, returning a deep copy of `self.mask` in this scenario. This ensures that when one operand has a mask and the other doesn't, the existing mask is properly propagated to the result, which matches the expected behavior from v5.2.\n\nAll original test cases from the PR now work correctly:\n- Operations between two unmasked objects return no mask (None)\n- Operations between a masked object and an unmasked object (constant or NDData) properly propagate the existing mask\n- Operations between two masked objects work as before\n\nThe fix maintains backward compatibility and passes all existing tests in the nddata module.",
        "final_verification": {
          "checks": [
            "cd /testbed && python -c \"import numpy as np; from astropy.nddata import NDDataRef; array = np.array([[0, 1, 0], [1, 0, 1], [0, 1, 0]]); mask = np.array([[0, 1, 64], [8, 0, 1], [2, 1, 0]]); nref_nomask = NDDataRef(array); nref_mask = NDDataRef(array, mask=mask); # Test all cases from original PR result1 = nref_nomask.multiply(1., handle_mask=np.bitwise_or).mask; assert result1 is None; result2 = nref_nomask.multiply(nref_nomask, handle_mask=np.bitwise_or).mask; assert result2 is None; result3 = nref_mask.multiply(1., handle_mask=np.bitwise_or).mask; assert result3 is not None; result4 = nref_mask.multiply(nref_mask, handle_mask=np.bitwise_or).mask; assert result4 is not None; result5 = nref_mask.multiply(nref_nomask, handle_mask=np.bitwise_or).mask; assert result5 is not None; # Verify masks are correctly preserved assert np.array_equal(result3, mask); assert np.array_equal(result5, mask); print('All PR test cases pass!')\"",
            "cd /testbed && python -m pytest astropy/nddata/mixins/tests/test_ndarithmetic.py -q",
            "cd /testbed && python -m pytest astropy/nddata/tests/ -x --tb=short -q"
          ]
        }
